## New finding B3-1 (nonblocking Major)

A valid symlink under docs/ with a relative target survives the
preview.sh dangling scan and the publish drift check. Probe facts:

- docs/rel-alias.html -> ../outside.html. The docs side resolves to
  <repo>/outside.html (H1). The preview copy resolves the same string to
  <repo>/.tmp/outside.html (H2).
- preview-base.json pinned H1. The approval row carried H2. The drift
  check passed. Publish exited 0 and overwrote the outside file with H2.
- A ../../ link wrote /tmp/opencode/deep-write.txt, two levels above
  docs/.
- A directory symlink failed closed: exit 2,
  `publish: drift dirlink/link-target.html`.
- A control run with no symlink wrote only the two approved rows into
  docs/.

Phase 1 cannot reach B3-1. The d14becb tree holds no tracked symlink and
no publish-approval.md, so publish always exits 2 today. The fix must
land before the Phase 5 first publish.

